ferences in mean TESS or QOL-CS scores, self-perception of disability, or scoring below the 25th percentile on QOL-CS or TESS scores were found after adjusting for general health, gender, educational status, and age at questionnaire completion (data not shown).</p><p>Poor general health status, older current age, and failure to graduate from high school predicted self-perception of disability and lower TESS and QOL-CS scores and were all statistically significant in univariate analyses (<xref rid="tbl4" ref-type="table">Table 4</xref><table-wrap id="tbl4" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Odds ratio for considering themselves disabled (moderately, severely or completely disabled) or having a TESS or QOL-CS score below the 25th percentile</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th colspan="3" align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold>Univariate</bold><hr/></th><th colspan="3" align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold>Multivariate</bold><hr/></th></tr><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Subgroups</bold></th><th align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold>Self-rating disable</bold></th><th align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold>TESS score</bold></th><th align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold>QOL-CS score</bold></th><th align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold>Self-rating disable</bold></th><th align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold>TESS score</bold></th><th align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold>QOL-CS score</bold></th></tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td align="left" valign="